      "id": 4,
      "options": {"reduceOptions": {"calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false}, "orientation": "auto", "textMode": "auto"},
      "targets": [{"expr": "sum(increase(ray_serve_deployment_replica_starts_total{job=\"ray\",application=\"aml\",deployment=\"AMLAPI\"}[15m]))", "refId": "A"}],
      "title": "Replica starts (15m)",
      "type": "stat"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "short", "decimals": 0}, "overrides": []},
      "gridPos": {"h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 7},
      "id": 5,
      "targets": [
        {"expr": "sum(ray_serve_deployment_replica_healthy{job=\"ray\",application=\"aml\",deployment=\"AMLAPI\"})", "legendFormat": "healthy replicas", "refId": "A"},
        {"expr": "max(ray_serve_autoscaling_target_replicas{job=\"ray\",application=\"aml\",deployment=\"AMLAPI\"})", "legendFormat": "autoscaler target", "refId": "B"},
        {"expr": "max(ray_serve_autoscaling_desired_replicas{job=\"ray\",application=\"aml\",deployment=\"AMLAPI\"})", "legendFormat": "raw desired", "refId": "C"}
      ],
      "title": "Autoscaler decision vs running replicas",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "short", "decimals": 0}, "overrides": []},
      "gridPos": {"h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 7},
      "id": 6,
      "targets": [{"expr": "sum by (replica) (ray_serve_replica_processing_queries{job=\"ray\",application=\"aml\",deployment=\"AMLAPI\",replica=~\"$replica\"})", "legendFormat": "{{replica}}", "refId": "A"}],
      "title": "Concurrent work by replica",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "reqps"}, "overrides": []},
      "gridPos": {"h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 16},
      "id": 7,
      "targets": [{"expr": "sum by (replica) (rate(ray_serve_deployment_request_counter_total{job=\"ray\",application=\"aml\",deployment=\"AMLAPI\",replica=~\"$replica\",route!~\"/metrics|/health\"}[1m]))", "legendFormat": "{{replica}}", "refId": "A"}],
      "title": "Request throughput by replica",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "s"}, "overrides": []},
      "gridPos": {"h": 9, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 16},
      "id": 8,
      "targets": [{"expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le, replica) (rate(ray_serve_deployment_processing_latency_ms_bucket{job=\"ray\",application=\"aml\",deployment=\"AMLAPI\",replica=~\"$replica\"}[5m]))) / 1000", "legendFormat": "{{replica}}", "refId": "A"}],
      "title": "p95 model processing latency by replica",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "short", "min": 0, "max": 1, "decimals": 0}, "overrides": []},
      "gridPos": {"h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 25},
      "id": 9,
      "targets": [{"expr": "ray_serve_deployment_replica_healthy{job=\"ray\",application=\"aml\",deployment=\"AMLAPI\",replica=~\"$replica\"}", "legendFormat": "{{replica}}", "refId": "A"}],
      "title": "Replica lifecycle (1 = healthy, 0 = stopped/unhealthy)",
      "type": "state-timeline"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {"type": "prometheus", "uid": "prometheus"},
      "fieldConfig": {"defaults": {"unit": "reqps"}, "overrides": []},
      "gridPos": {"h": 8, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 25},
      "id": 10,
      "targets": [{"expr": "sum by (replica, exception_type) (rate(ray_serve_deployment_error_counter_total{job=\"ray\",application=\"aml\",deployment=\"AMLAPI\",replica=~\"$replica\"}[5m]))", "legendFormat": "{{replica}} — {{exception_type}}", "refId": "A"}],
      "title": "Model exceptions by replica",
      "type": "timeseries"
    },
    {
      "gridPos": {"h": 7, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 33},
      "id": 11,
      "options": {"content": "## Reading replica behavior\n\nA traffic spike raises **queued/executing requests** first. The autoscaler's desired/target line then rises, followed by the healthy-replica count as new model processes finish loading. Throughput should spread across replica IDs. After demand falls, Ray waits for the configured downscale delay and removes idle replicas until one remains. A new replica ID in the lifecycle panel indicates a scale-up or replacement.", "mode": "markdown"},
      "title": "What to expect",
      "type": "text"
    }
  ],
